  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I have defined a [user config](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp#configuration) for yt-dlp in which I've specified the `-o` flag. After doing this, video players stopped working. It seems that when VRChat calls `yt-dlp`, yt-dlp finds that I have a user configuration and includes the flags I have defined, as shown by the output log:\n\n```\n\n2023.05.24 22:35:00 Error      -  [Video Playback] \n\nUsage: --no-check-certificate [OPTIONS] URL [URL...]\n\n--no-check-certificate: error: no such option: -o\n\n```\n\nAfter removing my user config, video players worked again.\n\nI believe that a potential solution would be to add the `--ignore-config` flag to the command.",
